title: 'Gnomon field run, day 2: voice like typing, Rules, MCP servers, git verbs, and a deny-by-default sandbox'
summary: |-
  The founder's live use of Gnomon (voice-only builds in a-platform-fighter) drove a batch merged into feat/gnomon, each part Mika- and Aegis-reviewed:
  - Voice:
    - the AirPods VPIO restart loop is fixed;
    - speaker continuity is added;
    - the send word sends the whole draft (TD-2026-10-23-496);
    - voice-sent turns follow the run mode and Always rules (TD-2026-10-23-939).
  - Always rules: scoped Always (file, repo, 3-word prefix), and a standing grant forms rules (TD-2026-10-23-815).
  - Rules view: off for a time, one save.
  - MCP servers: Paradigm's MCP is on by default; the human's servers are enabled by card (TD-2026-10-23-361); a batch card covers several servers with one presence.
  - Git: kernel-run git verbs over a kernel MCP channel (init, push, repo create, worktrees).
  - Sandbox: Aegis found the session profile was allow-default for writes (T-2026-10-23-004). It is now deny-by-default, with:
    - per-session caches and TMPDIR;
    - credential stores read-denied, and agent sockets and the keychain helper denied;
    - pinned push config and pinned shas.
  - Two kernel races fixed: drain vs exit work, and shutdown vs the push-config capture.
