    rationale: The founder explicitly accepted the bystander risk
  - id: TD-2026-10-23-815
    decision: A standing grant forms Always rules
    rationale: Always didn't stick under standing; the founder types passwords
  - id: TD-2026-10-23-361
    decision: Honor the human's MCP allow rules and run the linked Paradigm live
    rationale: The founder's choice over Aegis's force-ask and pinning
learnings:
  - Gnomon's session sandbox was allow-default for writes; every 'deny X' finding was a symptom. Audit the default before adding denies.
  - Builders running in parallel worktrees merge cleanly when each one owns distinct files; clientApiId pins and the GUI bundle hash always conflict and must be recomputed after the merge.
  - Unawaited startup work in the daemon (refreshPushConfig) showed up as an unrelated test flake; teardown races hide in afterEach errors.
  - 'The founder''s consistent principle: don''t gatekeep what they knowingly opted into. Make it visible, not blocked.'
